{
  "configuration_id": "config_005",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_002 (pca_n2000, multiprofile, avgpool) achieved the best result so far (acc 0.591, F1 0.573), substantially outperforming the single-profile baseline (config_001, 0.485) and the transformer aggregation (config_003, 0.519). Image-only models are very weak (0.208). The only RNA encoder tested is PCA (linear, 2000-dim). Uncertainty: We do not yet know whether the RNA representation itself is a meaningful design lever, or whether the profile/aggregation choices dominate. Question: config_005 (scvi_n200, multiprofile, avgpool) is a clean single-variable change from config_002, swapping the linear PCA encoder for a learned non-linear variational representation at 200 dimensions. This isolates the effect of RNA encoder while holding the best-known profile and aggregation fixed. Why this is the best next experiment: If scvi_n200 matches or beats PCA, it reveals that learned representations add value and justifies further encoder exploration (scgpt) and multimodal combinations. If it underperforms PCA, it strongly suggests the linear structure is sufficient, allowing us to rule out an entire family of configurations (005–009 and their multimodal counterparts) and redirect budget toward fusion or image-encoder questions. Either outcome reduces uncertainty about a core design axis with a single experiment."
}

